-- comments
1:1 plain -- `>` and `}` cannot stand in text (language.md §11.4): each is one
2:1 plain -- `invalid` token with unexpected_token, whose message gives `{">"}` and
3:1 plain -- `{"}"}` (6:10, 6:14), and the text resumes after each; the parser skips
4:1 plain -- them.
